# p05 the assay ran and produced no datum
#
# LinkML option: none. The repo's crosswalk (docs/crosswalk.md, cause c) puts this outside the
# six options because it is a fact about a process, not about a field.
#
# Live discussion: https://github.com/obi-ontology/obi/issues/1230
#   "Provide patterns for relating absence of actionable data with assay 'successfulness'"
#   (open since 2020-09-06). Positions recorded there, read 2026-09-14:
#   - 2020-09-14 OBI dev call: assays are understood and asserted to be completed planned processes.
#   - 2020-09-28: "intends to implement" is not an object property in OBI or COB; consensus to
#     request one in COB.
#   - 2026-04-06: NMDC uses COB:0000082 'planned process' for runs that can fail, because
#     COB:0000035 'completely executed planned process' is too narrow.
#   - 2026-04-07: RO:0002214 'has prototype' proposed as the link from a failed process to a
#     prototypical completed one; objection that its definition is about anatomical prototypes,
#     and a counter-position that the shared plan specification is the real link, with support
#     for a dedicated relation shaped like 'has prototype' that says so. No resolution recorded.
#
# What exists today (checked 2026-09-14): COB:0000083 'failed planned process' (subclass of
# COB:0000082, disjoint with COB:0000035 in COB 2025-12-15 and OBI 2026-07-27) and
# COB:0000085 'intended plan process type', an object property with a label and no definition,
# domain, or range. Whether COB:0000085 is the "intends to implement" relation requested in
# 2020 is not stated anywhere I read. It is used here as the closest existing term, pointing at
# the assay class by punning.
#
# Consequences of the current axioms, shown by ROBOT (README):
#   - The run cannot be typed OBI:2100072 'venous blood glucose assay': every assay is a
#     COB:0000035, which is disjoint with COB:0000083.
#   - It cannot use OBI:0000293 'has specified input': its domain is COB:0000035. So the
#     specimen is linked with RO:0000057 'has participant'. See p05_failed_assay_contradiction.ttl.
#
# A consumer can infer that a glucose assay was attempted on this specimen during this encounter
# and did not complete, so there is no datum to look for. They cannot infer why it failed.

@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:   <https://example.org/encounter/> .
@prefix BFO:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_> .
@prefix RO:   <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_> .
@prefix OBI:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_> .
@prefix COB:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_> .

ex:glucoseAssay1 a owl:NamedIndividual , COB:0000083 ;
    rdfs:label "failed glucose assay run 1" ;
    COB:0000085 OBI:2100072 ;              # intended plan process type (punned class)
    BFO:0000050 ex:encounter1 ;
    RO:0000057 ex:specimen1 , ex:provider1 .
    # no OBI:0000299 has specified output
